8. BARCODE AND QR CODE SYSTEM
==================================================

Implement a complete barcode identification workflow.

IMPORTANT BUSINESS RULE:

A QR code is NOT required on every product.

Most packaged grocery products already have a manufacturer barcode.

The system must support:

A. EXISTING PRODUCT BARCODES

When a cashier scans a barcode:

1. Read the scanner input.
2. Validate the scanned value.
3. Search the registered barcode database.
4. Identify the correct product.
5. Retrieve the configured selling price.
6. Add the product to the current cart.
7. Update inventory only after a successful sale.

Support common retail barcode formats, including EAN-13 and UPC-A, where applicable.

Do not assume a barcode contains the product's price.

The Family Mart database must determine the selling price.

B. PRODUCTS WITHOUT BARCODES

If a barcode is not found:

- Show a clear "Product Not Found" message.
- Keep the cashier on the POS screen.
- Offer product search.
- Allow searching by name or SKU.
- Allow selecting a matching product.
- Allow authorized staff to create a product from the product management module.
- Do not automatically create duplicate products from unknown scans.

C. INTERNAL BARCODE GENERATION

Authorized users must be able to generate internal barcodes.

Example:

Product: Family Mart Loose Sugar

SKU: FM-SUG-001

Internal barcode: Generate a unique valid code appropriate for the selected barcode format.

The example SKU is illustrative.

Generate a unique code and check for collisions before saving it.

Provide:

- Barcode preview.
- Printable labels.
- Product name.
- SKU.
- Optional selling price.
- Configurable label size.
- Print quantity.
- Batch label printing.

Internal barcodes must not be represented as official manufacturer barcodes.

D. QR CODE SUPPORT

Support QR-based product identification only when a QR payload is explicitly registered and the scanner can read it.

Do not treat arbitrary website URLs as product identifiers.

Keep product identification separate from customer payment QR codes.

If customer QR payments are implemented, create a separate payment workflow and only mark a payment as verified when appropriate confirmation is obtained.

E. UNKNOWN BARCODE HANDLING

When an unknown barcode is scanned, display:

"Barcode not registered. Search for the product or ask an authorized user to register it."

Provide clear actions:

- Search Product.
- Cancel.
- Open Product Management, if authorized.

