Financial calculations must follow clearly documented definitions.

Net Sales:
Eligible sales revenue after discounts and returns, using a clearly defined tax treatment.

Cost of Goods Sold:
The recorded inventory cost associated with sold items, calculated using a documented cost method.

Gross Profit:
Net Sales excluding applicable sales tax, minus Cost of Goods Sold.

Estimated Operating Profit:
Gross Profit minus recorded operating expenses.

Do not confuse total revenue with profit.

Do not count unreceived purchase orders as received inventory.

Do not count failed or cancelled sales as completed revenue.

Handle refunds, discounts, returns, and missing product costs correctly.

If cost data is missing, flag the report rather than silently reporting an incorrect profit.

Provide date filters and CSV export.

If Excel export is implemented, generate a valid Excel file.

